Rules:
  [P1] Use streaming replication for high availability.
  [P2] Use Patroni or repmgr for automatic failover.
  [P3] Use Citus for horizontal sharding.
  [P4] Use logical replication for multi-tenant architectures.
  [P5] Use point-in-time recovery (PITR) for backup.
  [P6] Use `pg_hba.conf` for access control.
  [P7] Use row-level security for multi-tenancy.
  [P8] Use PostGIS for geospatial data.

Pros:
  - High availability
  - Horizontal scaling
  - Data safety

Cons:
  - Operational complexity
  - Cost
  - Learning curve

Alternatives:
  - CockroachDB (distributed)
  - AWS Aurora (managed)
  - MongoDB (flexible schema)

State: +

